  "summary": "Strict matching leaves four GNN-style applications: message passing over relational graphs used for predicting protein molecular function. [V0145] is strongest and most dataset-aligned, reporting accuracy 0.92 on ProtMap. [V0148] reports F1 0.78 on MetroFlow and [V0147] reports AUROC 0.71 on ChurnBench. [V0146] is also an exact method-topic match but reports an error metric, FireScope MAE 0.64, so it is not directly comparable with the higher-is-better classification scores. The fifth ID, [V0156], is included only because five IDs were required: it has the same protein-function topic and reports MetroFlow MAE 0.65, but its stated method is decentralised training without pooled records rather than a graph neural network.",
